course: dictionary
lesson: 7105
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, so you need context to find the right one. «A pearl so precious a merchant sells everything for it» uses pearl to mean a very precious thing, not a shell. The words «sells everything» show how valuable it must be.
explain: Pearl can also be a colour. In «pearly white teeth», pearly means pale and shiny, like a real pearl. Here the clue is the word white. Pearly is the adjective form, so it describes something, just as shiny describes a coin.
explain: A pearl is also a real object, made inside a shellfish. Caddis fly larvae use sand and shells, and «an artist once gave them gold flakes and pearls». The word pearls there is the real thing, so read each sentence and ask which meaning fits.
fact: A pearl is a small, hard, shiny, round thing that grows inside an oyster or some other shellfish.
fact: A pearl forms when a grain of sand or another irritant gets inside an oyster, and the oyster covers it in layers of shiny nacre.
fact: «Pearl» can mean a very precious or excellent thing, as in «a pearl of a book».
fact: «Pearls of wisdom» are wise sayings, often said as a joke.
fact: «Pearly» is the adjective form, and it means pale, shiny white.
exercise: In «a pearl so precious a merchant sells everything for it», what does pearl mean? | A kind of fish | A sandy beach | A small grey stone | *A very precious thing
exercise: «Her teeth were pearly white.» What colour does pearly suggest? | Bright red | *Pale, shiny white | Deep blue | Dark green
exercise: A pearl forms when what gets inside an oyster? | *A grain of sand | A tiny fish | A drop of rain | A piece of bread
test: «Pearls of wisdom» is a phrase. What does it mean? | Shells found on the beach | Strings of beads worn at a party | Sad stories about the sea | *Wise sayings, often said as a joke
test: If someone calls a book «a pearl of a book», what do they mean? | It is a short book | It is a book printed on shiny paper | *It is a very excellent book | It is a book about oysters
exam: In «pearly white teeth», what does pearly mean? | Shaped like a round ball | Full of sand and grit | *Pale, shiny white, like a pearl | Very old and cracked
